# linux_binder_idl version - the Binder SDK / AIDL toolchain revision this
# rdk-halif-aidl snapshot is built against.
#
# build_binder.sh checks out this git ref (commit, tag or branch) when it
# clones the toolchain. Keep it pinned so the committed module-local
# generated C++ always matches the generator that produced it.
#
# Pinned to release tag 2.7.0 (linux_binder_idl), which ships:
#  - protocol 8 by default on every toolchain, with BINDER_PROTOCOL=7|8 and
#    TARGET_BITNESS=32|64 as the switches (linux_binder_idl#68/#69/#72); the
#    old BINDER_IPC_32BIT and TARGET_LIB32_VERSION/TARGET_LIB64_VERSION are
#    still honoured but deprecated;
#  - servicemanager registering without requesting callers' security
#    contexts, so binder works under AppArmor (linux_binder_idl#90/#91);
#  - the Yocto reference recipe on Kirkstone (linux_binder_idl#87/#88), and
#    host/logger.py without colorama (linux_binder_idl#81/#89).
# Its AIDL generator emits #include <mutex> in Bp*.h (linux_binder_idl#59).
# Every HAL module's committed C++ already carries it; the frozen
# examples/aidl_versioning snapshots predate it and pick it up on regeneration.
# Previously 2.6.0, which shipped the AIDL surface dump & structural diff
# toolchain (linux_binder_idl#27/#48) consumed by the release audit gate
# (#633/#568).
#
# Override for a one-off build with:  BINDER_VERSION=<ref> ./build_binder.sh
2.7.0
